        ":question/problem": "What is the value of ${\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{{log}_{3}\u2061x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x?$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let $u={log}_{3}\u2061x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}\u20613}\\,\u27f9\\,\\operatorname{ln}\u20613\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{{log}_{3}\u2061x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}{log}_{3}\u2061x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}u\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}\u20613\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}\u20613{\\int }_{0}^{1}u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}\u20613\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}\u20613\\cdot (\\frac{{1}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{0}^{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}\u20613}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
